Defend the functional material account (@mat-functional-review: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @materials-engineering, #materials-engineering "../processing/From-a-required-material-state-to-a-process-chain.lingua#r_2YT5QPFN4WNNHJFV88PEW1NKJC") { r_4R7JDE29DY1T4CNRV4Y6PDYHM9
**Read:** Finish the books, graduate notes, problems and three studies assigned in this section. Return to shared physics and earlier material structure, equilibrium, kinetics and mechanics wherever an explanation remains implicit.

Explain how states, occupation, interactions, vibrations, defects, domains and interfaces connect to electrical, ionic, thermal, dielectric, optical and magnetic observations. Derive the working models with their assumptions. Reproduce the original two-band calculation independently, identify its limitations and distinguish evidence from fitted plausibility.

**Demonstrate:** Defend the three studies, including a changed-condition prediction, uncertainty, alternative explanations and revision. Explain a material-state tradeoff across several functions without collapsing it into a property list. A good account can state what remains unknown and what measurement would resolve it.

Continue into fabrication and state control: use the mechanical and functional mechanisms to explain how processing creates the material state and how that state is checked.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).

**Continue in materials engineering:** [From a required material state to a process chain](../processing/From-a-required-material-state-to-a-process-chain.lingua#r_2YT5QPFN4WNNHJFV88PEW1NKJC).

